{# Turning a document figure into text at ingest, so it is findable by search and
   answerable later without re-opening the image.

   Changing this changes the MEANING of a stored extraction. Extractions are cached by
   (sha256, profile, dossier_version), so a reworked prompt requires bumping
   DOSSIER_VERSION in backend/assets/dossier.py — otherwise the cache keeps serving
   extractions produced under the old wording as if they were current. #}
You are extracting a document figure into text so that it can be found by search and answered from later, without anyone re-opening the image.

Context around the image:
{{ context }}

Produce:
- caption: one line naming what this image IS. Prefer the document's own caption wording when the context supplies it.
- description: what the image shows and how to read it. State the subject, the axes or columns, and the units. Do not speculate beyond what is visible.
- transcription: EVERY piece of text visible in the image, verbatim, including axis labels, legends, units, and footnotes. If it is a chart or a table, also render the underlying values as a markdown table. This field is what lets a text-only model answer questions about the figure later, so completeness here matters more than brevity.
- tags: short topical keywords a person might search for.
- image_type: the closest category.
- answerable_questions: up to four questions this image can answer, phrased the way a user would actually ask them.
- confidence: how legible and complete your reading was, from 0 to 1. Report low confidence honestly when the image is blurry, cropped, or you cannot read the text — a low score sends it for re-extraction rather than into the index as fact.

Write in the language of the document. Never invent values you cannot see.
